\rules only html
/* The sidebar on a narrow screen (below the sidebar breakpoint of the theme), where it stands above
   the story river. The core widget $scrollable gives it inline overflow: auto and
   -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch. Safari on iOS makes such a scroll container a stacking context
   of its own, and the story river after it (position: relative) then paints over everything that
   reaches out of the sidebar - the dropdown of the search ends at the lower edge of the sidebar,
   behind the first tiddler. Here the sidebar has no height of its own and never scrolls, so it
   needs neither. Above the breakpoint the sidebar is fixed and scrolls; nothing changes there. */
@media (max-width: <$text text={{{ [{$:/themes/tiddlywiki/vanilla/metrics/sidebarbreakpoint}removesuffix[px]subtract[1]addsuffix[px]] ~[{$:/themes/tiddlywiki/vanilla/metrics/sidebarbreakpoint}] }}}/>) {
	.tc-sidebar-scrollable {
		overflow: visible !important;
		-webkit-overflow-scrolling: auto !important;
	}
}
